# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# DocuCare .gitignore
#
# Keeps secrets and generated/junk files out of GitHub.
# NOTE: node_modules is deliberately NOT ignored here - it is committed on purpose.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- Secrets: environment files (DB password, JWT secret, encryption key) ----
# Ignore every .env variant...
.env
.env.*
*.env
# ...but keep the safe templates so others know which variables to set
!.env.example
!.env.sample
!.env.template

# ---- Build output (regenerated by `npm run build` / `vite build`) ----
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Admin-uploaded website images (runtime data, not source) ----
backend/uploads/

# ---- Logs ----
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
logs/

# ---- Local database dumps / backups (may contain real patient data) ----
*.sql.bak
*.dump
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
# (prisma/migrations/*.sql are needed and stay tracked)

# ---- Operating system files ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Editor / IDE personal settings ----
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json

# ---- Test / coverage output ----
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# ---- Temp files ----
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
.cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# node_modules is committed ON PURPOSE.
# The generic rules above (dist/, build/, *.log, .cache/ ...) would otherwise also hide files
# inside packages - almost every npm package ships its code in a dist/ or build/ folder, so
# without this exception the pushed node_modules would be incomplete and broken.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
!**/node_modules/**
